Description: pvr: reuse the queue's internal sync objects
 Every job submitted by the queue gets new binary sync objects: two per
 graphics job (geometry and fragment signal), one per compute, transfer and
 query job, one per barrier or event wait stage and one per stage with
 semaphore waits. pvr_update_job_syncs() and the barrier code destroy them
 again as soon as a newer one replaces them. Under zink every submit thus
 creates and destroys sync objects (DRM_IOCTL_SYNCOBJ_CREATE,
 DRM_IOCTL_SYNCOBJ_DESTROY).
 .
 Keep released sync objects in a small per-queue free list and take from it
 before creating a new one. These sync objects are only ever used as the
 signal of a job or null job before anything waits on them, and both the
 kernel job signal and drmSyncobjTransfer() replace the fence of a binary
 sync object, so the old fence does not matter. A wait on the geometry
 signal from the partial render job of the same DRM_IOCTL_PVR_SUBMIT_JOBS
 resolves to the new geometry job, as it does for the render context's
 geom_to_pr_syncobj that is already reused for every split submit
 (pvr_drm_winsys_render_submit()). Waits that reference a sync object are
 resolved when the job or null job is submitted, and a sync object is only
 put back after it is no longer referenced by the queue. Event sync
 objects are owned by the event and are not pooled. All access happens in
 driver_submit under the queue lock; the free list is destroyed with the
 queue.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
